   "text": "I read the molecule as a PROTAC-type degrader in three parts: a VHL ligand, a PEG linker, and a pyrrolotriazine\u2013isoquinoline ligand.\n\n**VHL end**\n- The hydroxyproline carries a hashed OH. I took it as the standard (2S,4R) form.\n- The tert-leucine is drawn with a wedge, and I took it as the standard (S) form.\n- The 1-[4-(4-methylthiazol-5-yl)phenyl]ethylamide has a wedged methyl. I assigned it by matching the standard VH032-type SMILES.\n\n**Linker**\n- From the tert-leucine NH the chain runs C(=O)\u2013CH2CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2CH2\u2013NH.\n- I counted three ether oxygens in the drawing.\n\n**Other end**\n- The linker NH is attached at C6 of an isoquinoline.\n- C1 of the isoquinoline carries a 1,2-disubstituted benzene.\n- The benzene's second substituent is CH2\u2013NH, which is bonded to a pyrrolo[2,1-f][1,2,4]triazine.\n- The triazine has an isopropyl group on the pyrrole ring.\n- It also has an O-linked piperidin-3-yl group. The wedge on the piperidine carbon, with priorities O > C2 (next to N) > C4, gives (R). I checked that the SMILES chirality tag encodes R.\n\nSMILES: C[C@H](NC(=O)[C@@H]1C[C@@H](O)CN1C(=O)[C@@H](NC(=O)CCOCCOCCOCCNc2ccc3c(c2)ccnc3-c2ccccc2CNc2nc(O[C@@H]3CCCNC3)nc3c(C(C)C)ccn23)C(C)(C)C)c1ccc(cc1)-c1scnc1C"
